  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat percentage increase occurs when the campus population doubles in one month? The number of students on campus triples at the end of every month. There are 12 students on campus at the beginning of the year. Percentage increase is calculated relative to the original population.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Initial population: \\(12\\) students.\n\nAfter one month, the population triples:\n\n\\[\n12 \\times 3 = 36\n\\]\n\nThe increase is:\n\n\\[\n36-12=24\n\\]\n\nRelative to the original population, the percentage increase is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{24}{12}\\times 100\\% = 200\\%\n\\]\n\nThus, under the stated “triples” condition, the percentage increase is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{200\\%}\n\\]\n\n(If the population literally doubled, the increase would be \\(100\\%\\).)",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. The number of students on campus doubles at the end of every month.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Initial population: \\(12\\) students.\n\nAfter one month, the population doubles:\n\n\\[\n12 \\times 2 = 24\n\\]\n\nThe increase is:\n\n\\[\n24-12=12\n\\]\n\nPercentage increase relative to the original population:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{12}\\times 100\\% = 100\\%\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the percentage increase is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{100\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. There are 10 students on campus at the beginning of the year.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The initial population is \\(10\\) students.\n\nAfter one month, the population doubles:\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 2 = 20\n\\]\n\nThe increase is:\n\n\\[\n20-10=10\n\\]\n\nThus, the percentage increase is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{10}\\times 100\\%=\\boxed{100\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: the student population is multiplied by 2 after each completed month.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The initial population is \\(10\\) students.\n\nAfter one completed month, it is multiplied by \\(2\\):\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 2 = 20\n\\]\n\nThe increase is:\n\n\\[\n20-10=10\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the percentage increase relative to the original population is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{10}\\times 100\\%=\\boxed{100\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many students will be on campus after three completed months?",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Starting with \\(10\\) students and multiplying by \\(2\\) after each completed month:\n\n- After 1 month: \\(10 \\times 2 = 20\\)\n- After 2 months: \\(20 \\times 2 = 40\\)\n- After 3 months: \\(40 \\times 2 = 80\\)\n\nTherefore, after three completed months, there will be\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{80\\text{ students}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: A doubling means the new population is twice the original population.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "A doubling means multiplying the current population by \\(2\\). Starting with \\(10\\) students:\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 2^3 = 10 \\times 8 = 80\n\\]\n\nTherefore, after three completed months, there will be\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{80\\text{ students}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "GOOD: —\nBAD: —\nWATCH: \"I should also tell you: A doubling means\"",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many additional students would have joined campus by the end of May beyond the students present at the beginning of the year? One more thing you should know: the question concerns the number of students on campus by the end of May.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "From the beginning of the year to the end of May, \\(5\\) months are completed. The population doubles each month:\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 2^5 = 10 \\times 32 = 320\n\\]\n\nThe number of additional students is:\n\n\\[\n320-10=310\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{310\\text{ additional students}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
